  "scope": "Independent frozen gameplan, exact inventory and closure-runner design audit. No candidate/source edits or formal execution. Approval is not a closure status or runtime acceptance.",
  "blocking_findings": [],
  "assessment": [
    "All89 pinned files and the canonical compact file-list root match. Contract SHA matches652f1950fb7497df063e58ebd05b54b0363f1bd2358b84b0900055508ab9c806.",
    "Candidate source has22 theorem declarations with exact symbol coverage. Source digest, ordered theorem_types, exact_check_output and saved author-type-audit.log agree. The append theorem includes its complete structure-update type, and nonvacuous_context includes its complete concrete witness proposition; the previous session inventory truncation is absent.",
    "The runner anchors the original287 statements to the fixed final-287-v2 report and manifest root, checks generated claims against the original manifest, compares current formal source bytes with archived originals and permits only the specified aggregate image import. Read-only checks confirmed the recorded anchor hashes/status/count and original formal source agreement. The runner further requires current registries equal anchored exact statements before adding22 candidate claims.",
    "Two fresh directories build the preserved model plus candidate; candidate and other printed inventories are compared exactly, original112 propositions are checked by typed examples, every theorem receives an allowed-axiom audit, and deterministic artifacts/inventories/status/provenance are compared. Input/review/source/proxy continuity checks surround builds. All309claims remain conditional on declared Lean, verifier, OS and hash trust; no build was executed for this review.",
    "The abstract model establishes inventory membership/completeness, kind collision rejection and exact scoped base/head selection for a supplied snapshot. It does not establish PostgreSQL snapshot creation, RLS, canonical ID extraction or Java response decoding. read_preserves_durable and concurrent_commit_does_not_mix follow from the pure supplied-observation model; they are not proofs that the real transaction is read-only or shares a snapshot.",
    "The dedicated transaction sequence places SET TRANSACTION before scope SELECTs, treats the first scope SELECT as a possible snapshot point, and closes the successful transaction/connection before returning context and launching the existing fresh worker. Existing READ COMMITTED mutation/read paths remain distinct. Concurrent additions are consistently excluded or included according to the one snapshot; no fallback lookup can silently mix snapshots.",
    "Authority stays server-derived and RLS-scoped. Empty-ID and SOURCE requests still perform exact authorized base reads. headObserved is informational and cannot replace CAS, browser accepted state, commit validation or a current-authority check. Requested-only definitions and full-history collision detection retain existing ownership semantics without trusting arbitrary text/reference occurrences.",
    "The26 planned runtime checks cover snapshot barriers, SQL routing and isolation order, failure after transaction exit, output/request limits, Java closed-shape decoding, no partial maps, freshness, resource bounds and durable nonmutation. These are future finite evidence requirements; approval does not report them passed.",
    "Fresh JVMs, BuildIdentity scans, sandbox limits, reaping and durable recovery semantics remain intact. This avoids the unresolved reusable-session classloader/reset architecture. SQL including transaction control still traverses the pinned SQLeanParser path, without a direct database exception.",
    "Baseline HTTP p95 remains468.348787ms against strict300ms. Roughly80ms saved on nonempty-ID calls is explicitly an unproven estimate; history traversal remains and empty-ID requests already had one bridge. The unchanged100warmup/1000measured benchmark must retain all failures and the gate remains FAIL if the target is missed."
  ],
  "nonblocking_watchpoints": [
    "The model assumes the database key/inventory abstraction: malformed histories, duplicate revision uniqueness, historical artifact integrity, wire safe-integer bounds and byte encoding are adapter obligations rather than theorem conclusions.",
    "The runner marks witnesses heuristically by symbol name containing witness or fixture; nonvacuous_context is nevertheless compiled and axiom-audited as a required exact claim. Report this concrete witness explicitly when summarizing closure rather than using the heuristic witness count as an exhaustive witness inventory.",
    "No accumulating decoded history list should be introduced. Actual psycopg cursor buffering and peak memory must be measured under the inherited process limits; payload quotas do not bound RSS.",
    "Closure configuration declares no network use but OS/toolchain execution is trusted. Do not present this declaration or proxy PID continuity as proof of sandbox network enforcement or SQL behavior.",
    "Keep commercial, accessibility, cold-series and release readiness claims outside the model/benchmark result. All six exact approvals and two registered builds remain prerequisites before implementation."
  ],
  "commercial_release": "NO_GO",
